@@ -337,6 +337,8 @@ prompt, which the runner leaves unanswered. Either can follow a dispatch, so the
 
 `data` is command-specific. Common fields include snapshot nodes, text lookup results, gesture timing, visibility metadata, and screenshot or recording output details.
 
+Interaction successes may carry the additive `actuation` object. Its `version` is `1`; `targeting`, `geometry`, and `executor` name independent facts, with optional `executorDetail`, `coordinateFallback`, and `mechanismFallback` evidence. A runner-resolved selector tap reports the geometry its resolution used (`runner-element-frame` or `runner-expected-point`) and the injector that fired. A coordinate interaction reports only the runner-owned executor slice. A text write reports the keyboard executor and its entry route in `executorDetail`. Every field is independently optional on the wire: absence means unknown or not owned by that reporter, never a purer mechanism.
